				Ath.
				8.356e
			</span></i>,  (in signf. <i><span class="en">
				111
			</span></i>) <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				4.204
			</span></i>: acc. pl. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πώλυπας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Dsc.
					2.166
				</span></i>
			; also acc. pl. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πόλυπας</span></b>  and acc. and gen. sg. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πόλυπα, πόλυπος,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Paul.Aeg.
				6.25
			</span></i>:— the common <i>poulp</i> or <i>octopus,</i>
			Od.l.c., <i><span class="en">
				Thgn.
			</span></i> l.c., <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				524a3
			</span></i>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> of
			insects, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>PA</u>
				682a36
			</span></i>, al.; esp. of the myriapods, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>HA</u>
				531b29
			</span></i>,al. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>polypus</i> or <i>morbid excrescence in the nose,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Aff.</u>
				5
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>HP</u>
				9.13.6
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				7.106
			</span></i>, Poll.l.c. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>IV.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. βοτάνη,</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πολυπόδιον</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Gp.</u>
				15.1.14
			</span></i>.</div>
